    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Bruce Cockburn"
      },
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Bruce Cockburn"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Bruce Cockburn has enjoyed an illustrious career shaped by politics, spirituality, and musical diversity. His remarkable journey has seen him embrace folk, jazz, rock, and worldbeat styles while earning high praise as a prolific, inspired songwriter and accomplished guitarist. He remains deeply respected for his activism and humanist song lyrics that thread throughout his career. On all his albums, Cockburn has deftly captured the joy, pain, fear, and faith of human experience in song. Bruce Cockburn has won 13 JUNO Awards, been inducted into the Canadian Songwriters Hall of Fame, received a Governor General’s Performing Arts Award, and has been made an Officer of the Order of Canada, among many other accolades. He has 22 gold and platinum records, including a six-times platinum record for his Christmas album. Cockburn continues to tour internationally."
      },
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Bruce Cockburn mène une carrière exceptionnelle marquée par la politique, la spiritualité et une insatiable curiosité musicale. Folk, jazz, rock et musique du monde, il a tout exploré, s’imposant comme un auteur-compositeur à la fois inspiré et prolifique, et un guitariste virtuose. Figure respectée pour son engagement et la portée humaniste de ses textes, il a su capter avec finesse, album après album, les joies, les peines, les craintes et la foi qui traversent l’expérience humaine. Treize fois récompensé aux prix JUNO, il a été intronisé au Panthéon des auteurs-compositeurs canadiens, couronné aux Prix du Gouverneur général pour les arts du spectacle et nommé officier de l’Ordre du Canada. Avec 22 disques d’or et de platine à son actif – dont une certification sextuple platine pour son album de Noël – Bruce Cockburn continue de se produire un peu partout dans le monde."
      }
    ]
  },
