    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Gentiane MG is a Montreal pianist and composer known for emotionally resonant piano trio music that bridges contemporary jazz and classical influences. With her long-standing trio, she presents Can You Hear the Birds?, a project shaped by connection, listening, and shared human experience. The music explores themes of presence, resilience, forgiveness, and renewal, unfolding through intuitive interplay and collective improvisation. Rooted in an ear-based creative process, the trio’s performances are fluid, open, and deeply connected, inviting audiences into a space of attention, curiosity, and emotional clarity. The NAC would like to acknowledge the generous support of John and Pina Sicard."
      },
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Gentiane MG is a Montreal pianist and composer known for emotionally resonant piano trio music that bridges contemporary jazz and classical influence. With her long-standing trio, she presents Can You Hear the Birds?, a project shaped by connection, listening, and shared human experience. The music explores themes of presence, resilience, forgiveness, and renewal, unfolding through intuitive interplay and collective improvisation. Rooted in an ear-based creative process, the trio’s performances are fluid, open, and deeply connected, inviting audiences into a space of attention, curiosity, and emotional clarity. Le Centre national des Arts tient à souligner le généreux soutien de John et Pina Sicard."
      }
    ]
  },
